  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Offer four tap choices taken from the stem. Exactly one choice is the adjective that describes a noun.",
      "Keep one describing adjective in every stem. A second adjective makes two right answers.",
      "Wrong choices are the described noun, a verb or linking verb, and one other non-adjective stem word.",
      "Use kid places only: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands and no real names.",
      "Tier 1 distractors are far: the noun, a clear action, and a place or person word.",
      "Tier 2 may use a second noun or a linking verb. The adjective may come after is or are.",
      "Tier 3 must include an -ly adverb as a near-miss wrong choice. That -ly word is never the key.",
      "Never use an article as the key. Never invent a choice that is not in the stem."
    ]
  },
